(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[8 1 "// Descriptors (PY5c; CPython's Objects/descrobject.c, funcobject.c's classmethod and staticmethod,"] [9 1 "// classobject.c's method, typeobject.c's super and slot wrappers): bound methods, functions as"] [10 1 "// descriptors, classmethod, staticmethod, property, __slots__' members, super, the slot wrappers"] [11 1 "// that show a built-in type's slots as methods, and the attributes of types, functions and methods."] [24 1 "// Method is a bound method: a function and the object it is bound to."] [31 1 "// ClassMethod and StaticMethod wrap a callable."] [46 1 "// Property is property(fget, fset, fdel, doc)."] [50 27 "// a subclass of property"] [60 1 "// Member is a __slots__ entry's descriptor."] [69 1 "// Super is super(type, obj)."] [78 1 "// slotWrapper is a built-in type's slot as a method (wrapper_descriptor)."] [87 1 "// mappingProxy is a type's __dict__ read only."] [90 11 "// the type whose __dict__ it is, or nil"] [91 11 "// the mapping, when it is no dict (mappingproxy(UserDict()))"] [94 1 "// proxied is the mapping behind p."] [118 1 "// newWrappers are the built-in types' __new__ objects, one each."] [126 1 "// slotWrappers keep one wrapper per type and name, so that int.__repr__ is int.__repr__ (enum compares"] [127 1 "// a class's methods with its data type's and object's; PY5e, part 2b)."] [130 1 "// slotWrapperFor is built-in type m's slot for the special method name, or nil."] [157 2 "// the number protocol's binary methods (__add__, __radd__, __iadd__ ...): the Binary, RBinary and InPlace"] [158 2 "// slots, NotImplemented when they do not apply (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200: test_asyncio reads int.__add__)"] [183 6 "// wrap_ternaryfunc_r: the operands swapped, the modulus third"] [196 22 "// wrap_indexargfunc"] [207 4 "// object_str: tp_repr, never the type's own __str__ (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: a class with"] [208 4 "// __str__ = object.__str__, doctest's DocTestCase, recursed without end)"] [329 5 "// dict_subscript sees self's type: a subclass's d.__getitem__(k) calls its __missing__ as d[k] does"] [330 5 "// (queue 202: urllib.parse's _Quoter(safe).__getitem__ raised KeyError: test_http_cookies,"] [331 5 "// test_wsgiref's request_uri)"] [439 3 "// one object per type, so that object.__new__ is object.__new__ (enum's _find_new_ compares them;"] [440 3 "// PY5e, part 2b)"] [492 29 "// unicode__format__: an empty spec, a subclass's str()"] [526 1 "// hackCheck is hackcheck: m's __setattr__ called on self, whose built-in base nearest to its type overrides it"] [527 1 "// (object.__setattr__(str, ...) would jump over type's own)."] [537 22 "// of the built-in bases one can reach here, only type overrides tp_setattro"] [544 1 "// objectDir is object.__dir__: the instance's dictionary's keys and its class's attributes."] [591 3 "// object's wrappers are made on demand (slotWrapperFor), add_operators' names here"] [614 1 "// superArgs are super()'s zero arguments: the running function's first argument and its __class__ cell."] [652 2 "// supercheck: a proxy's __class__ (a class it pretends to be an instance of)"] [682 2 "// functions as descriptors, bound methods"] [689 2 "// types.MethodType(func, instance) (method_new)"] [715 2 "// method_descr_get: a bound method is not bound again (gh-113157)"] [754 2 "// slot wrappers"] [785 2 "// classmethod, staticmethod (funcobject.c): a subclass's instance is an Instance around the Go value, so every"] [786 2 "// slot unwraps; __init__ copies the wrapped callable's attributes (functools_wraps) into the dict"] [889 3 "// descriptor_get_wrapped_attribute and its setter: the dict first, the callable's value kept there"] [934 2 "// property"] [1066 2 "// __slots__' members"] [1147 2 "// super"] [1194 5 "// a built-in type's method, or a method descriptor in a heap type's dict (methodDescrs: _ast's AST,"] [1195 5 "// queue 202c: super().__init__ in a node class's subclass)"] [1223 53 "// a subclass of super: its type called"] [1245 2 "// mappingproxy"] [1247 2 "// mappingproxy(mapping), over a dict (PY6a: enum's __members__); other mappings are the data model's"] [1258 3 "// mappingproxy_check_mapping: PyMapping_Check, not a list or a tuple"] [1268 2 "// a built-in type's own slots' wrappers (ownSlots, registry.go) are in its __dict__ too (PY5e, part 2b)"] [1276 14 "// a built-in type's attribute descriptors (type.__dict__['__annotations__']: annotationlib)"] [1308 2 "// mappingproxy_richcompare: the mapping's own comparison (queue 202: mappingproxy({}) == {} was False; test_re's"] [1309 2 "// test_getattr compares a pattern's groupindex with a dict)"] [1334 2 "// mappingproxy_or: the mappings beneath, a proxy's unwrapped on either side"] [1457 21 "// inside the first mro()"] [1507 2 "// type_get_text_signature: the signature in tp_doc, for the types that have one here (func_new's clinic doc)"] [1518 33 "// type_mro: mro_implementation afresh, a metaclass's mro() builds on it"] [1569 1 "// checkSetSpecial is check_set_special_type_attr."] [1751 2 "// __module__ is func.go's (PY6d's R5: the function's module), which this init's order let override this one"] [1754 1 "// excSlots are the __slots__ values of exceptions (an exception class's instances are *Exception, not"] [1755 1 "// *Instance): PY6a, by the integration's owner, for test_exceptions' slotted exception classes."] [1758 1 "// setTypeBases is type.__bases__'s setter (typeobject.c's type_set_bases; PY6b's request: typing.NamedTuple"] [1759 1 "// assigns a class's bases): a heap type's bases replaced by types of the same instance layout, its MRO and its"] [1760 1 "// subclasses' computed again and their slots refilled."] [1779 3 "// a reentrant mro() has not set base's MRO yet: its __base__ is asked too"] [1805 2 "// nothing more when a reentrant assignment replaced the bases"] [1824 1 "// newStaticBase is tp_new_wrapper's staticbase (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_bad_new): t, or"] [1825 1 "// the first base along __base__ whose __new__ is not a Python class's own (slot_tp_new)."] [1833 1 "// newOrigin is the built-in type whose __new__ t's tp_new is (inherited along __base__ from the first one"] [1834 1 "// that defines it), CPython's tp_new pointer compared."] [1848 1 "// newAliases: the built-in types whose own __new__ here is CPython's inherited one (defaultdict's is dict_new)"] [1851 1 "// isNewWrapper: v is a built-in type's __new__ (tp_new_wrapper); a class whose __new__ is one keeps the"] [1852 1 "// __new__ it inherits (update_one_slot's special case), so that class C(list): __new__ = object.__new__"] [1853 1 "// makes lists"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[133 29] [151 37] [191 37] [195 34] [209 67] [220 63] [225 68] [230 67] [246 37] [263 37] [285 37] [292 38] [324 37] [328 25] [342 38] [347 37] [357 37] [380 37] [418 38] [423 37] [441 26] [455 29] [482 25] [484 38] [491 34] [505 37] [530 12] [530 22] [551 24] [553 24] [576 24] [594 31] [646 26] [657 24] [664 23] [707 34] [710 36] [720 54] [722 57] [745 55] [759 27] [797 26] [804 41] [817 40] [852 22] [872 27] [894 24] [965 38] [973 28] [975 56] [1015 42] [1041 50] [1051 53] [1056 48] [1057 26] [1068 26] [1075 31] [1076 32] [1085 22] [1091 26] [1095 31] [1122 26] [1129 26] [1135 26] [1141 26] [1150 43] [1189 51] [1196 29] [1202 36] [1233 29] [1239 29] [1252 38] [1255 30] [1274 23] [1275 36] [1291 25] [1303 31] [1336 32] [1376 47] [1392 51] [1405 39] [1413 48] [1416 23] [1428 34] [1434 45] [1449 25] [1468 43] [1478 47] [1492 26] [1502 25] [1602 22] [1606 46] [1608 25] [1612 49] [1614 27] [1631 29] [1648 29] [1676 29] [1689 27] [1726 23] [1737 30] [1745 28] [1763 46] [1789 62] [1795 34] [1796 25] [1796 33] [1836 23] [1859 34]]} (go/file "descr.go" :imports [


